+Creating STRICT tables
+----------------------
+
+SQLite 3.37 and higher supports ``STRICT`` tables, which reject values that do
+not match the declared column type. Pass ``strict=True`` to ``db.create_table()``
+or ``table.create()`` to create one::
+
+    db["people"].create({"id": int, "name": str}, pk="id", strict=True)
+
+Python ``float`` columns are created as ``REAL`` in STRICT tables. You can also
+use the string types ``"INT"``, ``"INTEGER"``, ``"REAL"``, ``"TEXT"``,
+``"BLOB"`` and ``"ANY"`` accepted by SQLite STRICT tables.
+
